1.35 Prove these.
(a) For any ⃗v ∈V, if ⃗w ∈V is an additive inverse of ⃗v, then ⃗v is an additive
inverse of ⃗w. So a vector is an additive inverse of any additive inverse of itself.
(b) Vector addition left-cancels: if ⃗v,⃗s,⃗t ∈V then ⃗v +⃗s = ⃗v +⃗t implies that ⃗s = ⃗t.
