under addition, note that if the summands satisfy that x1 + y1 + z1 = 0 and
x2 + y2 + z2 = 0 then the sum satisﬁes that (x1 + x2) + (y1 + y2) + (z1 + z2) =
(x1 + y1 + z1) + (x2 + y2 + z2) = 0. For closure under scalar multiplication, if
x + y + z = 0 then the scalar multiple has rx + ry + rz = r(x + y + z) = 0.
