IV.3
Mechanics of Matrix Multiplication
We can consider matrix multiplication as a mechanical process, putting aside for
the moment any implications about the underlying maps.


Section IV. Matrix Operations
245
The striking thing about this operation is the way that rows and columns
combine. The i, j entry of the matrix product is the dot product of row i of the
left matrix with column j of the right one. For instance, here a second row and
a third column combine to make a 2, 3 entry.
