To solve for this coeﬃcient, observe that because ⃗v −c⃗p⃗s is orthogonal to a
scalar multiple of ⃗s, it must be orthogonal to ⃗s itself. Then (⃗v −c⃗p⃗s) • ⃗s = 0
gives that c⃗p = ⃗v • ⃗s/⃗s • ⃗s.
1.1 Deﬁnition The orthogonal projection of ⃗v into the line spanned by a
nonzero ⃗s is this vector.
proj[⃗s ](⃗v) = ⃗v • ⃗s
