⃗v ∈V with ⃗v = ⃗m + ⃗n where ⃗m ∈M, ⃗n ∈N, the projection of ⃗v into M along
N is projM,N(⃗v ) = ⃗m.
This deﬁnition applies in spaces where we don’t have a ready deﬁnition
of orthogonal. (Deﬁnitions of orthogonality for spaces other than the Rn are
perfectly possible but we haven’t seen any in this book.)
