The above two squares are arrangements of 1 . . . n2. They are normal. The
1×1 square whose sole entry is 1 is normal, Exercise 2 shows that there is no nor-
mal 2×2 magic square, and there are normal magic squares of every other size; see
[Wikipedia, Magic Square]. Finding how many normal magic squares there are of
each size is an unsolved problem; see [Online Encyclopedia of Integer Sequences].
If we don’t require that the squares be normal then we can say much more.
Every 1×1 square is magic, trivially. If the rows, columns, and diagonals of a
2×2 matrix
 
a
