Laplace’s expansion formula reduces the calculation of an n×n determinant
to the evaluation of a number of (n −1)×(n −1) ones. Chiò’s formula is
also recursive but it reduces an n×n determinant to a single (n −1)×(n −1)
determinant, calculated from a number of 2×2 determinants. However, for large
matrices Gauss’s Method is better than either of these; for instance, it takes
roughly half as many operations as Chiò’s Method [Fuller & Logan].
