1.9 Example By uniqueness, if c(x) = m(x)·q(x) then where c(x) = (x−3)2(x+2)3
and m(x) = (x −3)(x + 2)2, we know that q(x) = (x −3)(x + 2).
While x2+1 has no real roots and so doesn’t factor over the real numbers, if we
