3.17 Deﬁnition Where a characteristic polynomial factors into (x −λ1)m1 · · · (x −
λk)mk then the eigenvalue λi has algebraic multiplicity mi. Its geometric
multiplicity is the dimension of the associated eigenspace Vλi.
In Example 3.16, there are two eigenvalues, For λ1 = 1 both the algebraic
and geometric multiplicities are 2. For λ2 = 0 both the algebraic and geometric
multiplicities are 1. In contrast, Example 3.14 shows that the eigenvalue λ = 2
has algebraic multiplicity 2 but geometric multiplicity 1. For every transforma-
