1.8 Deﬁnition Let t be a transformation on an n-dimensional space. The gen-
eralized range space (or closure of the range space) is R∞(t) = R(tn). The
generalized null space (or closure of the null space) is N∞(t) = N (tn).
This graph illustrates. The horizontal axis gives the power j of a transfor-
