Thus if c1 ̸= 0, as k increases the vectors T k⃗v will tend toward the direction
of the eigenvectors associated with the dominant eigenvalue. Consequently, the
ratios of the vector lengths |T k⃗v|/|T k−1⃗v| tend to that dominant eigenvalue.
