Usually when we pick representatives we have some natural scheme in mind. In
that case we call them the canonical representatives. An example is that two
fractions 3/5 and 9/15 are equivalent. In everyday work we often prefer to use
the ‘simplest form’ or ‘reduced form’ fraction 3/5 as the class representative.
