3.7
Glossary
• Probability mass function (PMF): a representation of a distribu-
tion as a function that maps from values to probabilities.
• probability: A frequency expressed as a fraction of the sample size.
• normalization: The process of dividing a frequency by a sample size
to get a probability.
• index: In a pandas DataFrame, the index is a special column that
contains the row labels.


