CDF(1) = 0.2
CDF(2) = 0.6
CDF(3) = 0.8
CDF(4) = 0.8
CDF(5) = 1
We can evaluate the CDF for any value of x, not just values that appear in
the sample. If x is less than the smallest value in the sample, CDF(x) is 0.


