5.6
Generating random numbers
Analytic CDFs can be used to generate random numbers with a given dis-
tribution function, p = CDF(x).
If there is an efficient way to compute
the inverse CDF, we can generate random values with the appropriate dis-
tribution by choosing p from a uniform distribution between 0 and 1, then
choosing x = ICDF(p).
For example, the CDF of the exponential distribution is
p = 1 −e−λx
Solving for x yields:
x = −log(1 −p)/λ
So in Python we can write
def expovariate(lam):


