Std(ys) is the standard deviation of the dependent variable, which is the
RMSE if you have to guess birth weights without the benefit of any explana-
tory variables. Std(res) is the standard deviation of the residuals, which
is the RMSE if your guesses are informed by the mother’s age. As we have
